    "kind": "certification",
    "proves": "Verify that all 5 node-agents remain active throughout a ~4 minute\nobservation window without operator intervention.\n\nThe node-agent is the executor for all cluster operations \u2014 if it\ncrashes and fails to restart, the node becomes unmanageable. This\nscenario samples all 5 nodes at 3 time points to verify:\n  - All node-agents are in \"active\" systemd state throughout\n  - No node-agent crash-loops during idle operation\n  - The installed package count (Layer 3) remains stable\n\nThis tests the \"quiet\" stability of the cluster: no chaos, no load,\njust time passing. If a node-agent exits during idle operation it\nindicates a memory leak, keepalive failure, or bad systemd unit config.\n\nAll 5 nodes are checked because founding nodes (1-3) and worker\nnodes (4-5) have different service footprints and different risk profiles.",
